## Critical rules the agent must follow
- Every table has an `owner_id`. Every query in every route MUST filter by the logged-in user's id from the JWT, except when the route is behind adminMiddleware.
- Never trust a client-reported payment as final — only the Razorpay webhook (signature-verified) may update `users.balance`.
- The webhook route for WhatsApp must respond to Meta within a few seconds (ack fast, process async) or Meta will retry/flag it.
- Category cost lookup (marketing/utility/authentication/service) must happen server-side at send time, never trust a cost value sent from the frontend.
- Use parameterized queries everywhere (mysql2 placeholders) — no string-concatenated SQL, to avoid injection.

